# In front of a loop that stores by name into an object that nobody knows stands the search of the property's address. The site of the store may say it: the code in front asks the site's record, for the structure and for a word of the object's own, and calls the search where it says anything else.
# function move(to, from, n) { for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { to.n = from.m; from.m = i; } }  sink(move);
